# prose-style.config — what counts as prose here, and what is deliberately not.
#
# Written 2026-09-04 during the repo-wide em-dash pass. Every `skip` and
# `region` below is a category that pass had to hold back, each for a reason
# that only shows up by reading the code. They are recorded here so the next
# pass does not have to rediscover them, and so nobody "finishes the job" by
# deleting an em dash that is load-bearing.
#
#   node prose-style.mjs --root . --check    # gate
#   node prose-style.mjs --root . --fix      # confident fixes only

rule   em-dash —

scan   **/*.md
scan   **/*.cff

# --- held back, with cause -------------------------------------------------

skip   bin/**                  # why: functional, bin/handover-lint.js:100 has an em dash inside /^(n\/a|-|—|none)$/i that recognizes a verify_cmd of "—" as "no command given"; removing it sends that value to the shell
skip   hooks/**                # why: same enforcement path as bin/
skip   bench/scenarios/**      # why: benchmark ground truth, the deterministic layer text-matches trap descriptions, so edits move the scores the paper reports
skip   examples/**             # why: examples/handover.example.md is asserted by the suite to lint VALID
skip   templates/**            # why: templates/handover.template.md is asserted to lint INVALID
skip   paper/**                # why: no PDF build path in the repo, so editing the HTML desyncs it from paper/handover.pdf, the artifact archived on Zenodo under the DOI

# --- guarded spans inside otherwise-scanned files --------------------------
# (lab-only; harmless here, kept so both repos can share one config)
region docs/ARXIV_SUBMISSION.md  ## Abstract::## Categories   # why: must byte-match the published PDF
